text:
MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "PTXmas and That's Christmas To Me combine Christmas music with the group vocal harmonies I want, making them natural next choices after my holiday albums and The New Old Fashioned.",
    "That's Christmas To Me felt especially relevant because it connects my repeated Christmas listening with my more recent interest in vocal harmony music."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Summer Horns offers instrumental music when I want voices blending together, while Viva Duets does not give me the same appeal as a harmony group.",
    "Older-hit collections, solo pop, and classic country do not clearly connect to what brought me back. Titles such as Stages and Passione also give me too little evidence of that connection to choose them during a rare visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to treat interest in a few vocal albums as interest in a much broader range of singers and musical styles.",
    "Some recommendations seemed to assume that an older or familiar collection would appeal to me, although familiarity alone is not what I am looking for."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of Christmas songs and group vocal harmonies matters more to me than either a general holiday connection or the presence of a singer alone.",
    "My Christmas interactions were clustered in one older visit, while The New Old Fashioned was more recent; I want the harmony connection carried forward rather than assuming every visit is only about Christmas."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations caught my interest in Christmas vocal harmonies but extended it too broadly to music without that clear connection."
}
